WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Two small boats side by side; one person may step across at a time,

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.800
and the boats may differ by one person at most.

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.661
The most eager may not go first.

4
00:00:14.661 --> 00:00:17.261
Someone else crosses first.

5
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.988
Five friends, two rooms; one person moves at a time.

6
00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:27.677
The rooms may differ by one at most. Gain: friends outside minus inside.

7
00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:31.677
Ada and Eva: 6 each, the biggest.

8
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.200
Move Ada? The left room would keep just one.

9
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.200
One to four is too lopsided: not allowed.

10
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.800
The same for Eva.

11
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.313
Among the legal ones, Dev is best: +3.

12
00:00:55.313 --> 00:00:58.780
Dev moves across: 12 → 9.

13
00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.780
Now the left room has three.

14
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.839
Now Ada may go: +6.

15
00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:09.239
9 → 3.

16
00:01:09.239 --> 00:01:12.928
Both lock for the rest of the round.

17
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Keep going, even at a loss:

18
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.800
Cai −2, Eva −6, Ben −1.

19
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.400
Back to 12: all of it trials.

20
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.400
The best prefix: the first two steps.

21
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.000
Roll back to 3.

22
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.522
Six others: at first every legal move loses.

23
00:01:47.522 --> 00:01:51.522
Take two small losses: 6 → 7 → 8.

24
00:01:51.522 --> 00:01:56.122
Then E gains 4: down to 4, the best split.

25
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.181
Back to the five: round two starts from 3.

26
00:02:03.181 --> 00:02:06.781
Every prefix is worse than staying put.

27
00:02:06.781 --> 00:02:09.781
The empty prefix wins: stop.

28
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.627
On a chip: the halves may differ a little; cells move one by one.

29
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.500
One at a time, the head count inside the window.

30
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.500
The biggest gain must be legal first.

31
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:40.500
Try the losses; keep only the best prefix.

32
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:48.500
What if distance matters, not ties? Next module.

33
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.600
In the lab below, see which moves the balance blocks.
